    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full `mvnw test` run passes with BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164:\n\n1. **`OwnerTelephone.java`** \u2014 made the class `public` and added a public static `toDisplay(String raw)` method. It canonicalizes the value to E.164, splits off the country code (using the existing recognized-country-code map, else groups everything after `+`), and groups the national digits in threes: `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. Values that can't form valid E.164 are returned unchanged.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema (so `OwnerDto` is generated with it), documenting the human format and noting `telephone` stays E.164.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that populates `telephoneDisplay` from `OwnerTelephone.toDisplay(owner.getTelephone())`.\n\nThe response layer (`RespondWithOwner`/mapper) already flows through this, so the acceptance test \u2014 asserting `telephone` = `+61412345678` and `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678` \u2014 passes, and the full suite is green.",
